{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/782313-judeo-christian-mythology-research","id":782313,"title":"Judeo-Christian Mythology Research","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-08T08:20:15-08:00","id":782313,"title":"Judeo-Christian Mythology Research","content":"Anyone know of any good books on Judeo-Christian Mythology? I'm looking for less Angels with Wings and Halos and more Lilith being the mother of demons type stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:23:20-08:00","id":782338,"title":"","content":"For starters, try a translated version of the Talmud. After that, I'd suggest going the esoteric route, as I'm guessing you're using this for gaming. A look at the medieval Grimoires (most available as scanned pdf online, if you look around): The Lesser Key of Solomon or Lemegeton, for a popularized medieval look at terminology and occult thought involving demons and such. There are countless books written by historians about Lilith as everything from an archetype of feminine humanity to something akin to a feminized Jungian Shadow.<br /> <br /> I'll look up a few old favorite books/resources and update this. Sometime today, if nobody else has things to add.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:33:12-08:00","id":782346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/782313-judeo-christian-mythology-research?p=782338#post782338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For starters, try a translated version of the Talmud. After that, I'd suggest going the esoteric route, as I'm guessing you're using this for gaming. A look at the medieval Grimoires (most available as scanned pdf online, if you look around): The Lesser Key of Solomon or Lemegeton, for a popularized medieval look at terminology and occult thought involving demons and such. There are countless books written by historians about Lilith as everything from an archetype of feminine humanity to something akin to a feminized Jungian Shadow.<br /> <br /> I'll look up a few old favorite books/resources and update this. Sometime today, if nobody else has things to add.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is exactly what I am looking for. My ADD mind is going back to an old idea I had after reading an article about the Catholic Church using Atheist Scientists to confirm that potential miraculous event do not have a scientific explanation before the church officially declares something a Miracle. I wanted to pull ideas from about Angels and Demons from older Judeo-Christian Traditions instead of the current &quot;Touched by an Angel&quot; mythology of today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:34:12-08:00","id":782349,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry if this comes off as a bit unhelpful... but:<br /> <br /> Step 1: Don't use the phrase Judeo-Christian.<br /> <br /> I know it is a fairly common phrase, but it is incredibly biasing when you're trying to look up information on two highly divergent sets of mythologies. It draws you towards a selection that's biased towards specific European narratives, rather than looking at either Christian mythology or Jewish mythology as wholes in their own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:44:46-08:00","id":782354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/782313-judeo-christian-mythology-research?p=782349#post782349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry if this comes off as a bit unhelpful... but:<br /> <br /> Step 1: Don't use the phrase Judeo-Christian.<br /> <br /> I know it is a fairly common phrase, but it is incredibly biasing when you're trying to look up information on two highly divergent sets of mythologies. It draws you towards a selection that's biased towards specific European narratives, rather than looking at either Christian mythology or Jewish mythology as wholes in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hmmm... That may be part of my problem with my research. Wrong keywords. I'll keep that in mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:47:16-08:00","id":782356,"title":"","content":"Heavy has a point, and I'd like to build on it a bit: The history of both Jewish religious mythology and Christian mythology were flavored by neighboring theologies and legends. Zoroastrianism has a basic equivalent to angels, developed during the same time period as Abrahamic traditions, and in the same general region of the globe. The modern Cherub or Cherubim type angel commonly referred to in Angelology is though to originate with the Zoroastrian Kherub. Both traditionally depicted more like griffins or certain dragons than a chubby baby with wings. It's worth noting that Enochian &quot;angel magic&quot;, like that associated with the Enochian alphabet, sometimes refers directly to cherubs as Kherubim. The physical descriptions of angels or angelic figures in actual scripture should be noted as well. The Old Testament has some trippy descriptions for the angels witnessed; wheels of fire with eyes, three-faced beasts, etc.<br /> <br /> The idea of winged men as angels, by contrast, is relatively new and mostly an idea popularized by early religious art where the artist used wings to symbolically denote a figure's celestial origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 12-08-2015, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T10:13:59-08:00","id":782366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/782313-judeo-christian-mythology-research?p=782349#post782349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry if this comes off as a bit unhelpful... but:<br /> <br /> Step 1: Don't use the phrase Judeo-Christian.<br /> <br /> I know it is a fairly common phrase, but it is incredibly biasing when you're trying to look up information on two highly divergent sets of mythologies. It draws you towards a selection that's biased towards specific European narratives, rather than looking at either Christian mythology or Jewish mythology as wholes in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are the same family of mythologies, together with Islam. Same as Greek and Roman mythology are in the same family. It's a fair categorization. There is no implication of equality, but they are branches of the same tree.<br /> <br /> I prefer Abrahamic mythology as a term, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T13:45:38-08:00","id":782475,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to deny their common history. I also prefer the phrase Abrahamic (especially as there are more than just the three religions in that tree, even if the other branches are very small in both size, and influence on the others).<br /> <br /> The problem with Judeo-Christian as a categorization is that while there are cases where it can fairly apply, there are two issues. First, from an academic stand point, as noted above, it can be very unhelpful because it focuses on the parallel religious histories of primarily European Jews and Christians, while reducing or ignoring the influence of the same parallel histories for Jews living in Muslim, Zooastrian, and other religion dominated parts of the world. Second, from a more... evangelical I guess is the best word for it... perspective Judeo-Christian is often used to mean, &quot;Christian stuff that acknowledges Judaism as the past,&quot; that tries to bias more neutral academic studies with the narrative that Christianity is the current Abrahamic faith, and Judaism is the obsolete past that needs to get brought up to speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T03:39:36-08:00","id":823204,"title":"","content":"I am not Hindu but I don't say Hindu mythology but Hindu religion because there are still millions of people who believe it.<br /> <br /> Other matter about saints with &quot;supernatural powers&quot; don't work like magic from fiction or real-world ocultism. In the Christian religion the &quot;charismas&quot; are sacred gift to help community, it isn't an art or skill you can learn reading a book or practice in a workshop.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is to learn more is reading &quot;Life of Jesus&quot; by Maria Valtorta. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T11:55:14-08:00","id":823572,"title":"","content":"Mythology and religion aren't the same thing. Studying mythology is generally studying the intersection of theology and sociology (though not all mythology studies formal religious beliefs). It's not just about what a group of people believe, but how their stories teach/inform their beliefs and norms between generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:15:35-08:00","id":823593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/782313-judeo-christian-mythology-research?p=823204#post823204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not Hindu but I don't say Hindu mythology but Hindu religion because there are still millions of people who believe it.<br /> <br /> Other matter about saints with &quot;supernatural powers&quot; don't work like magic from fiction or real-world ocultism. In the Christian religion the &quot;charismas&quot; are sacred gift to help community, it isn't an art or skill you can learn reading a book or practice in a workshop.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is to learn more is reading &quot;Life of Jesus&quot; by Maria Valtorta.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/782313-judeo-christian-mythology-research?p=823572#post823572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mythology and religion aren't the same thing. Studying mythology is generally studying the intersection of theology and sociology (though not all mythology studies formal religious beliefs). It's not just about what a group of people believe, but how their stories teach/inform their beliefs and norms between generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms has the right idea. I started this topic to find out more about the more mythological elements of Abrahamic Religions than the more spiritual/ethical side that is taught in Church/Temple/Mosque. I grew up Catholic and went to Catholic school, so I know all about the life of Jesus and his miracles. I was never taught about Lilith, Lucifer, hierarchy of angels, etc. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:33:20-08:00","id":823782,"title":"","content":"To expand even further, Lilith isn't an official part of Judaism. She isn't in the Tanach (though there is a fairly late reference to &quot;unclean&quot; animals in Isiah that includes lilit that seems more in line with Babylonian/Sumerian mythology of the same name). She doesn't play into any of the rituals, symbolism, or beliefs of the mainstream of the religion. However she's been a fairly significant figure in Jewish folklore and mythology for some time.<br /> <br /> You can study formal Jewish theology for decades and never touch on Lilith in any significant detail because she doesn't really matter at all to it. However she's very significant to Jewish mythology. She's a strong link between Jewish and neighboring cultures, the stories about her play heavily into Jewish folklore about demonology and protective/warding superstitions, etc.<br /> <br /> There's a lot you can learn about Jewish culture in different eras by studying the Lilith mythology at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T04:00:34-08:00","id":824893,"title":"","content":"Wait a moment, Judaism and Christian religion is a thing, and popular folklore from Jewisch comunity and Christian culture is a different thing.<br /> <br /> Maybe you can something in wikipedia<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Christian_folklore\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catego...stian_folklore</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Jewish_folklore\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Jewish_folklore\" target=\"_blank\"> Category:Jewish folklore - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Jewish_folklore\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Jewish_folklore </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Jewish_legendary_creatures\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catego...dary_creatures</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:20:35-08:00","id":825018,"title":"","content":"Mythology is an intersectional subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}